==English==

===Etymology===
Partly from {{bor|en|nl|Noorsch}} (now {{m|nl|Noors}}), from {{m|nl|noordsch|t=northern; nordic}}; and partly from {{bor|en|da|norsk|t=Norse}}. Both equivalent to {{af|en|north|-ish|nocat=1}}. {{doublet|en|Norsk}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{enPR|nôrs}}, {{IPA|/nɔɹs/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/nɔːs/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-Norse.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-uk-Norse.ogg|Audio (UK)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɔː(r)s|lang=en}}

